# Movement speed (server/README.md "Movement speed"; client base-patch 0029 predicts the same steps, change both together):
#  1. Base speed: vocation base + playerSpeedBonus (50) + playerSpeedPerTenLevels / 10 (2.5) per level up to
#     playerSpeedSoftLevel (300), then playerSpeedPerTenLevelsAbove / 10 (1) per level (stock: vocation + 2 per level).
#  2. A player's walk speed (base + haste, slows, items, mounts, passive tree, Paragon, Lua changeSpeed) is held between
#     minPlayerSpeed (120, about 1 tile/s: a slow never freezes a player) and maxPlayerSpeed (2600, 100 ms = 10 tiles/s on
#     normal ground). Staff with PlayerFlag_SetMaxSpeed keep the stock limits; 0 turns a limit off. Monsters unchanged.
#  3. A player's step is rounded up to 10 ms (stock: the 50 ms beat, which turned a 107 ms step into 150 ms) and a
#     diagonal step takes 7/5 of a straight one (this engine's stock code meant 1.5 but stored it in an integer, so the
#     server walked diagonals at 1x while the client waited 3x). Monsters and NPCs keep 50 ms and their 1x diagonal.
#  4. The step formula no longer wraps to a 0 ms step below speed 16 (step speed at least 1, as the stock code meant).
# Lua: creature:getStepSpeed() (the clamped speed), configKeys.MIN_PLAYER_SPEED, MAX_PLAYER_SPEED, PLAYER_SPEED_BONUS,
# PLAYER_SPEED_PER_TEN_LEVELS, PLAYER_SPEED_SOFT_LEVEL, PLAYER_SPEED_PER_TEN_LEVELS_ABOVE; mirror: data/lib/chaos_speed.lua
# (tests/movement_speed_test.lua). Apply in the server source root after 0001-0017: patch -p1 < 0018-movement-speed.patch
